Fix torch 2.13.0 ROCm build against aotriton 0.11.x (nixpkgs pins 0.11.1b).
All changes are version-guarded on AOTRITON_VERSION_CURRENT and confined to
USE_ROCM / !DISABLE_AOTRITON regions, so CUDA and CPU-only builds are
unaffected.

- aten/src/ATen/native/transformers/hip/aotriton_adapter.h: in the
  pre-0.12 branch, acquire() receives the LazyTensor cookie directly as
  its `self` argument (0.11's LazyTensor stores a bare void* cookie), so
  casting the undeclared `cookie` identifier fails to compile. Use `self`.
- aten/src/ATen/native/transformers/cuda/attention_backward.cu and
  transformers/hip/flash_attn/aot/mha_all_aot.hip:
  attn_options::deterministic only exists in aotriton >= 0.12; guard the
  assignments so 0.11 builds (determinism falls back to default off, same
  as the CK backend path).
- transformers/hip/flash_attn/aot/mha_all_aot.hip: VarlenType::StridedVarlen
  and attn_fwd_params::seq_strides_q/k are 0.12+ only. On 0.11, reject the
  strided-varlen path (seqused_k) with TORCH_CHECK instead of silently
  miscomputing; plain dense/compact varlen attention is unaffected.
